    {
      "id": "751f81bcda5e7fdf9bf0bb8a89d937523a1ae4db",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2343149388,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It looks like this broke the OSS-Fuzz builds. When I follow the instructions at https://google.github.io/oss-fuzz/advanced-topics/reproducing/ I end up with binaries that are dynamically linked to libglib-2.0.so.0, which isn't installed. Adding a debugging `message` to `FindGLIB2.cmake` shows the following:\n\nPC_GLIB2_FOUND: 1\nGLIB2_LIBRARY: /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libglib-2.0.a\nPC_GLIB2_STATIC_LIBRARIES: glib-2.0;pcre\nPC_GLIB2_STATIC_LDFLAGS_OTHER: -pthread\n\nThe container is based on Ubuntu 20.04.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1788825804",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-02-12T00:00:21.939Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-02-12T00:00:21.939Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 356945321,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 18820,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0cc2c9ebf772e9765a3b19a63cc3cfb6bb7b95e0",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2343176307,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Ok, I will give it a look. That's when giving `-DOSS_FUZZ` so that `USE_STATIC` gets set? I could imagine how this would lead to the wrong libraries when linking statically if something was wrong, but it shouldn't have changed whether the dynamic or static library was preferred.\n\nThough some odd results can happen if you have only the dynamic library installed but ask for static (and the pkg config file is still there.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
