      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2343234929,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I followed the instructions at that page, then ran \n\n`python infra/helper.py shell wireshark`\n\nwhich brought me to an image where:\n```shell\nroot@e67443616865:/work/build/run# cd /work/build/run\nroot@e67443616865:/work/build/run# ls -l\ntotal 1159844\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 root root         0 Feb 12 01:56 extcap\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 root root 366641304 Feb 12 01:58 fuzzshark\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 root root   9164440 Feb 12 01:57 lemon\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root   4108778 Feb 12 01:57 libui.a\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root 797493746 Feb 12 01:58 libwireshark.a\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root   8827604 Feb 12 01:57 libwiretap.a\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root   1426370 Feb 12 01:57 libwsutil.a\nroot@e67443616865:/work/build/run# ldd ./fuzzshark \n\tlinux-vdso.so.1 =>  (0x00007fab1ba9b000)\n\tlibdl.so.2 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libdl.so.2 (0x00007fab1b5fc000)\n\tlibm.so.6 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libm.so.6 (0x00007fab1b2f3000)\n\tlibpthread.so.0 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libpthread.so.0 (0x00007fab1b0d6000)\n\tlibrt.so.1 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/librt.so.1 (0x00007fab1aece000)\n\tlibgcc_s.so.1 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libgcc_s.so.1 (0x00007fab1acb8000)\n\tlibc.so.6 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6 (0x00007fab1a8ee000)\n\t/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 (0x00007fab1b800000) \n```\n\nwith a fuzzshark that seems to work? Very possible I don't understand what I'm doing though.",
