          "id": 2343240025,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Though now that I'm looking at the OSS-Fuzz build (following those instructions here: https://google.github.io/oss-fuzz/advanced-topics/reproducing/), it seems to have built with CMake 3.5.1 and be looking for Lua 5.1 or 5.2, and definitely not building against a version of Wireshark that would have this commit in it.\n\nBut if I follow the instructions to use a more recent source path `$ python infra/helper.py build_fuzzers  --sanitizer <address/memory/undefined> $PROJECT_NAME <source_path>` then the build halts with a CMake error about 3.16 or higher being required. Though since it's saying CMake 3.5.1, that would be Ubuntu Xenial, which doesn't seem right, even though I ran `$ python infra/helper.py pull_images` as instructed.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-02-12T02:26:29.702Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-02-12T02:26:29.702Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 356945321,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
