    {
      "id": "9f1822ec2fc67447da955e019e58bdb1992316cb",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2343255311,
          "type": null,
          "body": "If I run `python infra/helper.py shell wireshark`, the latest commit in src/wireshark is e8a8056a6b, from yesterday.\n\nIf I run `python3 infra/helper.py build_fuzzers --sanitizer address wireshark` followed by `python3 infra/helper.py reproduce wireshark fuzzshark_ip_proto-udp /tmp/clusterfuzz-testcase-minimized-fuzzshark_ip_proto-udp-5700125095165952` the `reproduce` command fails with\n\n    /out/fuzzshark_ip_proto-udp: error while loading shared libraries: libglib-2.0.so.0: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory\n\nPart of the output is a `docker run ... gcr.io/oss-fuzz-base/base-runner` command. If I copy that and run it, and run `ldd /out/fuzzshark_ip_proto-udp` inside the container it prints\n\n\tlinux-vdso.so.1 (0x00007ffeeeeb0000)\n\tlibdl.so.2 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libdl.so.2 (0x00007fc07d177000)\n\tlibglib-2.0.so.0 => not found\n\tlibm.so.6 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libm.so.6 (0x00007fc07d028000)\n\tlibpthread.so.0 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libpthread.so.0 (0x00007fc07d005000)\n\tlibrt.so.1 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/librt.so.1 (0x00007fc07cffb000)\n\tlibresolv.so.2 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libresolv.so.2 (0x00007fc07cfdf000)\n\tlibgcc_s.so.1 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libgcc_s.so.1 (0x00007fc07cfc2000)\n\tlibc.so.6 => /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6 (0x00007fc07cdd0000)\n\t/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 (0x00007fc07d183000)",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
