    {
      "id": "2d5f87bd60f808903423a3b5665d9c337d505e1b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2343258731,
          "type": null,
          "body": "For some reason the OSS-Fuzz python infra commands, even after I built a local wireshark image and tagged it, keep trying to download a five year old image from gcr.io/oss-fuzz/wireshark.\n\nOnce I figured my way around that, I get some CMake/ninja error trying to build the container using the version I tagged:\n```\nCMake Error:\n  Running\n\n   '/usr/bin/ninja' '-C' '/work/build' '-t' 'recompact'\n\n  failed with:\n\n   ninja: warning: bad deps log signature or version; starting over\n\n  ninja: error: failed recompaction: No such file or directory\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
